  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So I've played around with Avatar 3.0 all day and I've found some points that should probably be fixed in the SDK to improve usability.\n- Add a \"mood_neutral\" for the default facial puppet.  If you only have four blendshapes you might get a wierd default expression since it is trying to blend an average of all the shapes (this also makes it easier for people to set a default facial expression which might be different from the base model expression)\n\n- Create a default expression menu in examples (this seems to be missing?).  It's pretty easy to create a blank one, but it might be nice to have a default setup.\n\n- Rename some of the example controllers?  For example \"vrc_AvatarV3FaceLayer\" to \"vrc_AvatarV3FXLayer\", and vrc_AvatarV3HandsLayer to vrc_AvatarV3GestureLayer. This makes it easier to understand where these slot into.\n- Make notes in the Wiki to actually check out these examples, since most people should probably base their overrides off these.\n\nSDK Package \"VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2020.08.06.16.30\"",
